{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"Sessions","externalID":"Sessions","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey"},{"text":" to its session’s identifier. A session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes on while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The enricher tracks ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" before each session’s first event, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has no ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"kinds:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bits. The enricher holds it in memory only, and a new tracker, as on the next launch, starts a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session. A store keeps it beside each record of the session, and it is deleted when the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deletes the record’s bytes (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":": once its whole segment is delivered), so a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch still carries the session it was tracked in. The key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", is in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Events"},{"type":"text","text":" module."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, by the record’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enrichers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StandardContext"},{"type":"text","text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LifecycleTracking"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"tex